--- !u!114 &7626443560898476136
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 4589808537035243960}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d1e3fe6de7ae4c5a9a5ab17d081a6117, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::HelpApp
  appName: Help
  icon: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 6dc628ea7ff196e43adc1e15bdcf026a, type: 3}
  topics:
  - id: controls
    title: Controls
    body: '<b>WASD</b> move   <b>Mouse</b> look

      <b>Shift</b> sprint   <b>Space</b>
      jump   <b>Ctrl</b> crouch

      <b>F</b> use / pick up / put down   <b>Left
      click</b> place or click

      <b>Esc</b> phone   <b>Tab</b> notifications

      <b>1</b>
      price scanner   <b>2</b> paint brush

      <b>0</b> edit your store   <b>I</b>
      store checker

      <b>L</b> lock or unlock a door


      The prompt in the
      middle of the screen always says what <b>F</b> will do with what you''re looking
      at.'
    video: {fileID: 0}
    blocks: []
  - id: phone
    title: Your phone
    body: '<b>Esc</b> brings the phone up on its home screen, <b>Tab</b> straight
      onto your notifications. Esc again goes back to the home screen, then puts
      it away.


      <b>Notifications:</b> everything that''s happened to you and
      your store.

      <b>Help:</b> this. When something happens for the first
      time, a tip comes up in the corner: bring the phone up while it''s there and
      it opens here on that topic.

      <b>Lost & Found:</b> lost children and
      where their parents are.

      <b>Franchises:</b> franchise auctions (unlocks
      at a higher level).

      <b>Settings:</b> sound, mouse, display, and Reset
      help tips to see the tips again.'
    video: {fileID: 0}
    blocks: []
  - id: your-store
    title: Your store
    body: 'You start with a small store. Stand at its monitor and press F to order
      stock, buy upgrades, spend perk points and expand.


      Open your store
      so customers can come in; close it when you need the floor to yourself. Buy
      more stores as your level allows: walk up to one for sale and press F.


      Press
      <b>I</b> for the store checker: what customers think of your store and why.'
    video: {fileID: 0}
    blocks: []
  - id: ordering
    title: Ordering and deliveries
    body: 'Order from your store''s monitor. Stock comes in crates, each holding
      several of one product; furniture and decor come on their own.


      Everything
      arrives in your store''s shipment area once its delivery time is up. If there''s
      no room, it waits at the dock until there is. Deliveries are held for you for
      10 minutes; after that anyone can take them. Carrying another store''s delivery
      to them earns a help point.'
    video: {fileID: 0}
    blocks: []
  - id: stocking
    title: Stocking shelves
    body: 'Hold a crate and look at a shelf: <b>F</b> stocks one (the preview shows
      where), <b>G</b> takes one back into the crate. With empty hands, <b>F</b>
      takes one off the shelf.


      <b>R</b> turns the products, <b>T</b> lays
      them down. If a crate won''t go, the prompt says why.


      <b>Sharing a
      shelf:</b> stock a different product on a shelf that already has one and the
      shelf splits in two. A line shows where it''ll split before you do; which way
      depends on where you''re standing. Clothes hang on racks, folded things go
      on shelves.


      A crate with room left can be topped up with more of the
      same product.'
    video: {fileID: 0}
    blocks: []
  - id: placing
    title: Placing things
    body: 'Pick something up with <b>F</b>. A see-through preview shows where it''ll
      go; if it can''t go there, the prompt says why. Turn it with <b>,</b> and <b>.</b>
      and click to put it down.


      You can only place things in your own store.
      Things need something under them, can''t go inside other things, and must leave
      a way through your doors: customers who can''t get out are let out after a
      while, and it costs you experience.


      To move a lot at once, or to build,
      use store edit mode (<b>0</b>).'
    video: {fileID: 0}
    blocks: []
  - id: carts
    title: Carts
    body: 'Look at your store''s cart with empty hands and press <b>F</b> to push
      it, <b>F</b> again to let go. Anything you put in its bed rides along, so it''s
      the quick way to bring several crates from the dock.


      Carts stop against
      walls and shelves. Pull too far from a stuck cart and you let go. Only your
      team can use your carts.'
    video: {fileID: 0}
    blocks: []
  - id: prices
    title: Prices
    body: 'Press <b>1</b> for the price scanner and click something for sale. Type
      a price and press <b>Enter</b> for that one, <b>Shift+Enter</b> for every one
      of that product in the store. A price of <b>0</b> takes it off sale. Esc or
      right click cancels.


      Customers compare your price with what the item
      is really worth on the market: too high and they walk away (and shoplifters
      are more tempted), low and they buy more but you make less. Market prices move
      with events and seasons.'
    video: {fileID: 0}
    blocks: []
  - id: checkout
    title: The checkout
    body: 'Customers line up and put their things on the belt. Click each thing to
      scan it.


      <b>Card:</b> take the card, then swipe it in the reader.

      <b>Cash:</b>
      take the cash, count the change out of the drawer (the keypad can work it out
      for you), then confirm.


      A customer who waits too long walks off and
      leaves their things: click them to take them back to the shelves.'
    video: {fileID: 0}
    blocks: []
  - id: customers
    title: Customers
    body: 'Customers come in different kinds, each liking different things and caring
      more or less about price and how a store looks. What they can see through your
      windows and doors decides whether they walk in.


      Some come as groups
      or families and shop together: children stay with their parents. Inside, they
      look for what suits them at a fair price. Keep shelves full, decorate to suit
      what you sell, and keep lines short.


      How many come to the mall depends
      on seasons, events, and the mall''s reputation: broken lights and lost children
      nobody helped keep shoppers away.'
    video: {fileID: 0}
    blocks: []
  - id: shoplifters
    title: Shoplifters
    body: 'Some customers steal, more so when a price is well over what the item
      is worth. They won''t try it with a player close by watching. A theft may set
      off the alarm as they leave (Theft Resistance perks make that likelier).


      Look
      at a customer and press <b>F</b> to stop them and check their bag. A shoplifter
      drops what they took as crates at their feet: pick them up and put them back.
      Catching someone stealing from another store earns a help point.'
    video: {fileID: 0}
    blocks: []
  - id: editing
    title: Editing your store
    body: 'Press <b>0</b> to edit (the store closes while you do). Move the camera
      with <b>WASD</b>, turn with <b>Q</b>/<b>E</b>, drag things to move them, <b>R</b>
      to rotate, <b>Ctrl</b> to move freely, <b>Delete</b> to sell something back.


      <b>B</b>
      builds walls, <b>H</b> changes their height or shows the controls. Windows
      and doors slide along walls and cut their own holes. Your storefront must keep
      a door.


      Press <b>0</b> again to save.'
    video: {fileID: 0}
    blocks: []
  - id: painting
    title: Painting and colors
    body: 'Tap <b>2</b> (empty hands) for the paint brush; hold <b>2</b> for the
      color wheel, point at a color and let go. Click something of yours to paint
      it: items that can be painted, walls, the storefront, the floor. Each paint
      job costs a small fee.


      Colors unlock as your team levels up. Some items
      only come in certain colors, and a franchise adds its own colors to the items
      it covers. Customers like some colors better on some things, and some kinds
      of customer have favorite colors.'
    video: {fileID: 32900000, guid: f9db0f538152532418cff906625e967e, type: 3}
    blocks: []
  - id: levels
    title: Levels and perks
    body: 'Happy customers and profit level your team up, unlocking items, colors,
      decor and more stores. Unhappy customers cost experience.


      Each store
      earns its own perk points from profit; spend them on its monitor''s Perks tab.
      You can respec for free, but a store whose layout doesn''t match its perks
      sells less.'
    video: {fileID: 0}
    blocks: []
  - id: licenses
    title: Licenses
    body: 'Some categories need a license before you can order them, and only so
      many licenses exist per mall. Get one from your monitor while there''s one
      free.


      Giving up a license you never ordered anything with earns a help
      point (someone else can use it).'
    video: {fileID: 0}
    blocks: []
  - id: franchises
    title: Franchises
    body: "A franchise makes your team the only one allowed to order its category
      for a while, and adds the brand's colors to its items.\n\nFranchises are won
      at auction: phone \u2192 Franchises (unlocks at a higher level). The highest
      bid when the auction ends wins. When it runs out, or its holder gives it up,
      bidding opens again."
    video: {fileID: 0}
    blocks: []
  - id: votes
    title: Mall votes
    body: 'Every so often a vote opens at the mall''s kiosks. Look at an option''s
      button and press <b>F</b> to vote (again to change your vote). When it closes,
      the winner changes the whole mall for a while.


      Help points make your
      vote count more: see Help points.'
    video: {fileID: 0}
    blocks: []
  - id: events
    title: Mall events and seasons
    body: 'Seasons run one after another, and events come and go on top of them.
      They change how many customers come and who, how much they spend, what things
      cost to order and sell for, even how many shoplifters there are.


      What''s
      running now is shown on screen. Stock up on what an event makes popular, and
      watch your prices when market prices move.'
    video: {fileID: 0}
    blocks: []
  - id: help-points
    title: Help points
    body: "Helping the mall earns help points:\n\u2022 bringing a lost child back
      to their family\n\u2022 reporting something broken\n\u2022 stopping a shoplifter
      in another team's store\n\u2022 delivering another store's order\n\u2022 giving
      up a license you didn't use\n\nEach kind only counts a few times per vote.
      Help points make your mall vote count more; the ones that did are used up when
      the vote closes."
    video: {fileID: 0}
    blocks: []
  - id: lost-children
    title: Lost children
    body: "Now and then a child wanders away from their family. Everyone's told,
      and the family stops shopping to look for them.\n\nPhone \u2192 <b>Lost & Found</b>
      shows a live picture of the child and of their parents, so you can work out
      where they are. Find the child and press <b>F</b>: they follow you. Stay close,
      or they'll lose you and wait where they stopped. Bring them to their parents
      for a help point and experience.\n\nA child nobody helps eventually finds their
      family alone, but word gets around: fewer shoppers come to the mall for a while."
    video: {fileID: 0}
    blocks: []
  - id: broken
    title: Broken lights and screens
    body: 'Things in the mall break now and then: a light flickers or goes out, a
      screen cracks. Broken things keep shoppers away from the whole mall, for as
      long as they''re broken.


      Spot one, look at it (from a distance is fine)
      and press <b>F</b> to report it: you get a help point and maintenance fixes
      it shortly. If nobody does, shoppers start complaining.'
    video: {fileID: 0}
    blocks: []
  topicButtonPrefab: {fileID: 0}
  backButtonPrefab: {fileID: 0}
